---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import { faqPageSchema } from '../schema/faqPage';

const meta = {
  title: 'Admissions Process | Start Recovery at Sunbright California',
  description:
    'A simple 4-step admissions process: call, assessment, plan your path, begin recovery. Your first call is private and free. Call 530-528-2342.',
  primaryKeyword: 'rehab admissions process',
  activeNav: 'admissions',
};

const breadcrumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
  { name: 'Admissions', url: '/admissions' },
];

const faqs = [
  {
    question: 'Is my call to Sunbright confidential?',
    answer:
      'Yes, completely. Your call is private and protected. We do not share your information with employers, family members, or anyone else without your explicit written consent. Federal law (42 CFR Part 2) provides additional confidentiality protections for people seeking addiction treatment beyond standard HIPAA rules. You can ask questions, share your situation, and explore options — with no obligation and no disclosure.',
  },
  {
    question: 'How soon can I start treatment?',
    answer:
      'We aim to move as quickly as a person is ready. After your initial call and clinical assessment, many people are able to begin within days. The exact timeline depends on bed availability and the outcome of your assessment. Call us at <a href="tel:+15305282342">(530) 528-2342</a> to discuss current availability.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Does Sunbright provide medical detox on-site?',
    answer:
      'Sunbright does not provide on-site medical detox. For individuals who require medically supervised withdrawal — which is common with alcohol, benzodiazepines, and opioids — we coordinate a referral to an appropriate detox facility before admission. Once medically cleared, the person can transition into our residential or outpatient program. Our admissions team will guide this process.',
  },
  {
    question: 'What does treatment cost?',
    answer:
      'Sunbright accepts private pay today. As a 501(c)(3) nonprofit, we are committed to making recovery accessible — but treatment is not free. Exact costs depend on the level of care and length of stay. Call us to discuss current rates and payment options. We do not want cost to be the reason someone cannot access care, and we will do our best to work with your situation.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Will my employer find out I went to treatment?',
    answer:
      'Not from us. Federal confidentiality law (42 CFR Part 2) prohibits us from disclosing that you are or were a client without your written consent. If you are using employer-provided insurance or FMLA leave, there may be separate disclosure considerations — your HR department or an employment attorney can advise on those specifics. But Sunbright will never contact your employer without your permission.',
  },
  {
    question: 'What should I bring to treatment?',
    answer:
      'After you are admitted, our team will send you a complete packing list. In general: comfortable clothing for about a week, personal hygiene items (no alcohol-based products), any prescribed medications in their original pharmacy bottles, a photo ID, and your insurance card if applicable. We will walk you through the full list during your assessment call.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Can family members be involved in the admissions process?',
    answer:
      'Yes, with your consent. Family members are often an important source of support during the decision to seek treatment. They are welcome to be part of calls and to ask questions. We also have a <a href="/family-resources">Family Resources page</a> with information to help loved ones understand addiction and the recovery process.',
  },
];
---

<SiteLayout {...meta} breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs} schema={[faqPageSchema(faqs)]}>
  <header class="page-header">
    <div class="wrap ph-inner">
      <span class="eyebrow">Admissions</span>
      <h1>Getting started is <em>simpler than you think.</em></h1>
      <p class="lead">You don't need to have everything figured out before you call. Our admissions process is built to be warm, clear, and low-pressure — four steps from your first call to beginning recovery.</p>
      <div class="btn-row">
        <a href="tel:+15305282342" class="btn btn-gold">Call (530) 528-2342</a>
        <a href="/insurance" class="btn btn-ghost">Insurance &amp; Payment</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section section--white">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div class="prose wide">
        <p>Deciding to reach out about addiction treatment takes courage. We want the process after that call to feel as uncomplicated and supportive as possible. There are no wrong questions, no judgment, and no pressure to commit to anything on the first conversation. Our admissions team — not a call center — answers the phone at Sunbright.</p>

        <h2>Who we serve</h2>
        <p>Sunbright Recovery Center is a <strong>16-bed co-ed nonprofit residential center</strong> in Red Bluff, California, serving adults throughout Northern California — including Redding, Chico, Sacramento, Tehama County, and surrounding communities. We treat <a href="/what-we-treat/alcohol">alcohol use disorder</a>, <a href="/what-we-treat/opioids">opioid addiction</a>, stimulant use, <a href="/what-we-treat/dual-diagnosis">co-occurring mental health conditions</a>, and <a href="/what-we-treat/trauma-addiction">trauma-rooted addiction</a>.</p>

        <h2>A note on medical detox</h2>
        <p>Sunbright does not provide on-site medical detox. If you or your loved one requires medically supervised withdrawal before entering residential care — which is often the case with alcohol, benzodiazepines, or opioids — we will help coordinate a referral to the appropriate detox setting. Once cleared, you can transition directly into our program. Our admissions team will walk you through every step of that coordination.</p>

        <h2>Privacy &amp; HIPAA</h2>
        <p>Your privacy is protected by HIPAA and by federal law (42 CFR Part 2), which provides some of the strongest confidentiality protections in healthcare specifically for people seeking addiction treatment. We do not share your information with employers, family members, or anyone else without your explicit written consent. Your call is between you and us.</p>
      </div>

      <aside class="aside">
        <h3>Admissions at a glance</h3>
        <div class="aside-row">
          <svg fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"/></svg>
          First call is private and free
        </div>
        <div class="aside-row">
          <svg fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"/></svg>
          No obligation to enroll
        </div>
        <div class="aside-row">
          <svg fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"/></svg>
          HIPAA + 42 CFR Part 2 protected
        </div>
        <div class="aside-row">
          <svg fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"/></svg>
          Private pay accepted today
        </div>
        <div class="aside-row">
          <svg fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"/></svg>
          Private pay accepted today
        </div>
        <div class="aside-row">
          <svg fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"/></svg>
          Red Bluff, CA — serving Northern CA
        </div>
        <a href="tel:+15305282342" class="btn btn-navy">Call (530) 528-2342</a>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--navy">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">The Admissions Process</span>
        <h2>Four steps from <em>your first call</em> to beginning recovery.</h2>
        <p class="lead">Every step is designed to be clear, compassionate, and easy to navigate — even when things feel overwhelming.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="steps grid-4">
        <div class="step">
          <span class="step-n">Step 01</span>
          <h3>Call Us</h3>
          <p>Call <a href="tel:+15305282342" style="color:inherit;text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:2px">(530) 528-2342</a> and speak directly with our admissions team — real people who know our program and care about getting you to the right help. There is no script, no sales pitch, and no pressure. Ask anything. We'll listen.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step">
          <span class="step-n">Step 02</span>
          <h3>Assessment</h3>
          <p>A brief clinical assessment helps us understand the full picture — substance use history, mental health, physical health, and what you've tried before. This is confidential, conducted by a trained clinician, and shapes the care plan that follows. It is also how we determine whether detox coordination is needed before admission.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step">
          <span class="step-n">Step 03</span>
          <h3>Plan Your Path</h3>
          <p>Based on your assessment, we'll recommend a level of care — residential (30, 60, or 90 days), IOP, PHP, or sober living. We'll also walk through the cost of care and private-pay options. We want you to have a clear picture before you commit to anything.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step">
          <span class="step-n">Step 04</span>
          <h3>Begin Recovery</h3>
          <p>When you're ready — and with everything in place — you arrive. Our team will welcome you, walk you through the center, introduce you to staff, and help you settle in. The first days are about safety, orientation, and beginning to build the foundation for what comes next.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--cream">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">What to Expect</span>
        <h2>Your first call, <em>in detail.</em></h2>
        <p class="lead">Most people feel relief after the first call — not because everything is solved, but because they no longer have to figure it out alone. Here is what the conversation looks like.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="features">
        <div class="feature">
          <div class="f-ic">
            <svg fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M3 5a2 2 0 012-2h3.28a1 1 0 01.948.684l1.498 4.493a1 1 0 01-.502 1.21l-2.257 1.13a11.042 11.042 0 005.516 5.516l1.13-2.257a1 1 0 011.21-.502l4.493 1.498a1 1 0 01.684.949V19a2 2 0 01-2 2h-1C9.716 21 3 14.284 3 6V5z"/></svg>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>We answer — no automated menus</h3>
            <p>When you call (530) 528-2342, you will reach a person familiar with our program. Not a call center. Not a voicemail chain. If we miss you, we call back quickly.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="feature">
          <div class="f-ic">
            <svg fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M8 12h.01M12 12h.01M16 12h.01M21 12c0 4.418-4.03 8-9 8a9.863 9.863 0 01-4.255-.949L3 20l1.395-3.72C3.512 15.042 3 13.574 3 12c0-4.418 4.03-8 9-8s9 3.582 9 8z"/></svg>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>You set the pace</h3>
            <p>There is no obligation to provide information you are not ready to share. We will ask what we need to assess fit, but we follow your lead. The conversation can be as brief or as detailed as you want it to be.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="feature">
          <div class="f-ic">
            <svg fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4m5.618-4.016A11.955 11.955 0 0112 2.944a11.955 11.955 0 01-8.618 3.04A12.02 12.02 0 003 9c0 5.591 3.824 10.29 9 11.622 5.176-1.332 9-6.03 9-11.622 0-1.042-.133-2.052-.382-3.016z"/></svg>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Honest answers about fit</h3>
            <p>If we are not the right match — because of clinical need, location, or anything else — we will say so and help you find the right resource. We would rather connect you with the right help than place you in the wrong program.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="feature">
          <div class="f-ic">
            <svg fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M12 8c-1.657 0-3 .895-3 2s1.343 2 3 2 3 .895 3 2-1.343 2-3 2m0-8c1.11 0 2.08.402 2.599 1M12 8V7m0 1v8m0 0v1m0-1c-1.11 0-2.08-.402-2.599-1M21 12a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z"/></svg>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Payment discussed openly</h3>
            <p>We will walk through the cost of care and your payment options on the first or second call — not at the end of a process. Sunbright accepts private pay today. Call to discuss what options are currently available.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--white">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">Levels of Care</span>
        <h2>Recovery at the right <em>intensity for you.</em></h2>
        <p class="lead">Your assessment determines which level of care is the right clinical fit. Here is a brief overview of what each level looks like at Sunbright.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid grid-3">
        <div class="card featured">
          <div class="card-tag">Residential</div>
          <h3>Inpatient Rehab</h3>
          <p>Live at our 16-bed center in Red Bluff for 30, 60, or 90 days. 24/7 clinical support, daily evidence-based programming, structured routine, and a therapeutic community. Best for those who need intensive support away from their current environment.</p>
          <a href="/programs/residential" class="card-link">About residential <svg fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg></a>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-tag">Outpatient</div>
          <h3>IOP &amp; PHP</h3>
          <p>Structured programming for several hours per day while living in the community. Often the right step-down from residential — or the appropriate starting level for those who do not need 24/7 care.</p>
          <a href="/programs/outpatient" class="card-link">About outpatient <svg fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg></a>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-tag">Aftercare</div>
          <h3>Sober Living</h3>
          <p>Structured, sober housing for people in early recovery who benefit from a supportive, accountable community environment as they re-engage with everyday life.</p>
          <a href="/programs/sober-living" class="card-link">About sober living <svg fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg></a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="callout" style="margin-top:36px">
        <svg fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M13 16h-1v-4h-1m1-4h.01M21 12a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z"/></svg>
        <p><strong>Not sure which level is right?</strong> That is exactly what the assessment call is designed to answer. Our clinical team uses ASAM criteria to match each person to the right level of care — you don't have to know in advance. <a href="tel:+15305282342">Call us and let's figure it out together.</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--gold">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">For Families</span>
        <h2>Calling on behalf of <em>a loved one.</em></h2>
        <p class="lead">You do not have to wait for someone to ask for help before reaching out to us. Family members call us every day — and we are glad they do.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="prose" style="margin:0 auto">
        <p>If your son, daughter, spouse, or parent is struggling with addiction, calling Sunbright is one of the most useful things you can do right now. We can help you understand what addiction is, what treatment looks like, how to have a conversation about getting help, and what our program offers — before your loved one ever picks up the phone.</p>
        <p>When your loved one is ready, the admissions process moves quickly. And the groundwork you lay now — knowing what to say, understanding what to expect — can make all the difference in that moment. Visit our <a href="/family-resources">Family Resources page</a> for guides, tools, and information designed specifically for people who love someone in active addiction.</p>
        <p>You can also <a href="/tour">schedule a tour</a> of our Red Bluff center so you have a clear picture of where your loved one would be living and healing.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--white">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">Admissions FAQs</span>
        <h2>Answers to the questions <em>people ask most.</em></h2>
      </div>
      <div class="faq">
        {faqs.map((faq) => (
          <details>
            <summary>{faq.question}</summary>
            <div class="faq-body" set:html={faq.answer} />
          </details>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cta-band">
    <span class="eyebrow">Red Bluff · Redding · Chico · Sacramento · Tehama County</span>
    <h2>Your first call is <em>private and free.</em></h2>
    <p>There is no obligation, no judgment, and no wrong time to call. Our admissions team is here to listen, answer your questions, and help you take the next step — at whatever pace is right for you.</p>
    <div class="btn-row">
      <a href="tel:+15305282342" class="btn btn-gold">Call (530) 528-2342</a>
      <a href="/insurance" class="btn btn-ghost">Insurance &amp; Payment</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
